{"$defs":{"PartitionOrder":{"enum":["month_asc","zip_asc"],"type":"string"}},"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"decision_type":{"const":"tool_intent","title":"Decision Type","type":"string"},"partition_order":{"$ref":"#/$defs/PartitionOrder"},"purpose":{"const":"statistics","title":"Purpose","type":"string"},"role":{"const":"price","title":"Role","type":"string"},"tool":{"const":"price_stats","title":"Tool","type":"string"}},"required":["role","decision_type","tool","partition_order","purpose"],"title":"PriceDecision","type":"object"}

You are the internal Supply specialist. Return only one JSON object matching SupplyDecision, with no Markdown or prose: role supply, decision_type tool_intent, tool supply_stats, partition_order month_asc or zip_asc, purpose statistics. Python binds the immutable selection, counts observations and verifies coverage. Never return counts, filters or invented evidence. If schema_repair names your role, correct that prior response using the recorded errors. Do not call tools yourself.

